+++ b/docs/audit/one_bar_nq_b0_b2_risk_comparison_20261012.md
@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+# B0 versus B2 risk comparison
+
+Status: **Historical accounting review complete. Exploratory. Not approved for live use.**
+
+## Question and result
+
+This review asks if B2's lower dollar result comes mainly from smaller exposure. The answer is **no for the full comparison**. B2 uses most of its declared stop-risk budget. B2 has weaker trade and risk-adjusted results after the MNQ listing date. Its lower contract exposure does reduce dollar losses in some periods, including 2026.
+
+B0 earned **$166,107.92** on 5,462 closed trades. B2 lost **$142,674.93** on 5,459 recorded closed trades across the full 2013–2026 history. B2's pre-May 6, 2019 results are counterfactual. MNQ did not exist then. On and after the launch date, both strategies use the same BID-only CFD proxy, not dated CME futures.
+
+| Period | Ledger | Trades | Net P&L | Win rate | Profit factor | Expectancy / trade | R expectancy / trade | Daily Sharpe | Calmar* |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| 2013–2026 | B0 | 5,462 | $166,108 | 47.8% | 1.267 | $30.41 | +0.0304R | 1.28 | 0.54 |
+| 2013–2026 | B2 | 5,459 | −$142,675 | 42.9% | 0.863 | −$26.14 | −0.0255R | −0.88 | −0.04 |
+| May 6, 2019–July 14, 2026 | B0 | 3,084 | $169,969 | 51.7% | 1.341 | $55.11 | +0.0551R | 1.87 | 1.50 |
+| May 6, 2019–July 14, 2026 | B2 | 3,079 | $104,069 | 49.3% | 1.208 | $33.80 | +0.0355R | 1.17 | 0.86 |
+| 2020–2025 | B0 | 2,586 | $178,830 | 52.4% | 1.441 | $69.15 | +0.0692R | 2.29 | 1.89 |
+| 2020–2025 | B2 | 2,582 | $112,699 | 50.3% | 1.281 | $43.65 | +0.0464R | 1.52 | 1.30 |
+| 2026 through July 14 | B0 | 238 | −$14,167 | 47.5% | 0.806 | −$59.53 | −0.0595R | −1.83 | −1.59 |
+| 2026 through July 14 | B2 | 237 | −$9,704 | 47.7% | 0.765 | −$40.95 | −0.0488R | −1.87 | −1.59 |
+
+R is closed trade net P&L divided by the ledger's ex-ante risk budget. B0 uses $1,000 per trade. B2 uses its saved `nominal_risk_usd`. A positive win rate does not imply positive expectancy. The tables show that B2's post-launch risk-unit expectancy is positive, but it is below B0's. In 2026 both are negative. B2 has a slightly less negative R expectancy and a slightly worse daily Sharpe.
+
+\* Calmar uses a fixed illustrative $1,000,000 starting balance. It uses the same daily P&L proxy described below. It is not a margin or account survivability result.
+
+## Is B2 undersized?
+
+B2's median nominal-risk use is **97.8%** of $1,000 over the full history, **95.6%** after MNQ launch, and **91.0%** in 2026. Mean use is 96.2%, 94.4%, and 89.9%, respectively. This does not show material underuse of its declared stop-risk budget.
+
+B2's median size is 8 MNQ for the full history, 6 MNQ after launch, and 3 MNQ in 2026. Those are 0.8, 0.6, and 0.3 NQ-equivalent contracts. This lower point exposure can explain why B2's 2026 dollar loss is smaller than B0's. It does not explain the weaker full-history or post-launch quality measures.
+
+As a non-native algebra diagnostic, the script scales each B2 trade's net P&L by `10 / actual MNQ quantity`. This estimates one NQ-equivalent exposure per trade and scales its recorded costs linearly. It produces **−$28,093** after launch and **−$48,435** in 2020–2025. B0 earned $169,969 and $178,830 in those same periods. In 2026, the same calculation produces +$10,778 even though B2's recorded result is −$9,704. This unstable result follows from variable sizing and trade outcomes. It does not support a claim that constant undersizing explains B2's result. The calculation is not a backtest. It ignores margin, market impact, and nonlinear execution costs.
+
+B2 also has higher recorded cost per trade: about **$39.84** after launch versus **$15.00** for B0. Across the full history the values are $82.53 and $15.00. B2 has variable contract quantity and per-contract fees. The fee and slippage assumptions are illustrative, and the BID-only source has no ASK or spread data.
+
+## Daily risk and Monte Carlo
+
+Closed trade net P&L is assigned to its **UTC entry date**. The daily series includes every calendar day, including zero-P&L days. It is not native mark-to-market equity. The full-history proxy has max drawdown of **−$21,212 (−2.12%)** for B0 and **−$263,421 (−26.34%)** for B2 on the illustrative $1m account. The B2 drawdown is dominated by pre-launch counterfactual size. Post-launch drawdown is −$17,184 for B0 and −$16,271 for B2. The proxy's ending equity and drawdown depend on shard completeness and must not be read as a funded account simulation.
+
+The moving-block bootstrap uses 5,000 paired resamples with circular blocks of 5 and 20 calendar days. It resamples B0 and B2 from the same sampled dates. It does not resample individual trades or assume normal returns.
+
+For the post-launch period, the 5-day block run gives median terminal P&L of **$169,767 for B0** and **$103,494 for B2**. The 5th–95th percentile ranges are $113,254–$225,614 and $49,090–$158,626. B2's paired annualized Sharpe difference has median **−0.70** and 5th–95th percentile range **−1.03 to −0.39**. B2 Sharpe exceeds B0 in 0% of these resamples. The 20-day block result is similar; B2 Sharpe is higher in 0.02% of resamples.
+
+For 2026, the 5-day block terminal P&L median is −$14,330 for B0 and −$9,809 for B2. B2's paired Sharpe difference has median −0.08, with a 5th–95th percentile range from −1.19 to +1.04. B2 Sharpe exceeds B0 in 44.9% of resamples. The interval is wide because 2026 has only 238 B0 and 237 B2 trades. Risk-unit bootstrap results and 20-day block sensitivity are in `monte_carlo.json`.
+
+The bootstrap describes resampled paths from observed history. It does not forecast future regimes. The post-launch sample still contains reviewed historical results, and 2026 is observed stress evidence, not a holdout. A $5,000 drawdown threshold is exceeded in all post-launch resamples for both strategies. This threshold is descriptive only.
+
+## Data checks and limits
+
+- The script read all 14 current annual B0 and B2 `evaluation_trades.csv` ledgers. It checked the B0 count and P&L against the latest practical-yearly report and checked B2 against the independent Phase 2–4 review.
+- The script checked B2 `r_multiple` against net P&L divided by saved nominal risk. It did not remove rows from the annual ledgers.
+- The B2 independent review found annual GTC boundary leakage, six out-of-year entry fills, and one entry fill duplicated across adjacent shards. The total ledger counts therefore preserve the observed shard outputs and may contain repeated or boundary-contaminated events.
+- The B2 costed path has 63 same-minute entry/stop ambiguities, one opposing-entry-order ambiguity, and 92 late scheduled exits. B0 has its own execution ambiguity. These historical path issues limit direct attribution.
+- The source is a Dukascopy BID-only USATECH index CFD proxy, not NQ or MNQ futures. No result is a live readiness claim. No unseen holdout exists.
+
+## Method and reproduction
+
+I loaded these local methodology skills and applied their checks:
+
+| Skill | Reason | Check applied |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ml4t-risk-metrics` | Compare risk-adjusted returns and drawdowns | Report Sharpe, Sortino, Calmar, drawdown, and risk-unit tails |
+| `ml4t-tearsheet` | Compare full performance rather than one metric | Report win rate, profit factor, expectancy, costs, drawdown, and Sharpe |
+| `ml4t-position-sizing` | Test whether B2 underuses its risk budget | Reconcile saved risk units and report quantity and budget use |
+| `ml4t-stress-test` | Evaluate observed 2026 adverse period | Keep 2026 separate and label it historical stress, not a holdout |
+| `ml4t-transaction-costs` | Separate gross sizing effect from cost burden | Report recorded fee and slippage burden; retain spread and impact limits |
+| `ml4t-polars-patterns` | Group ledger P&L by calendar day | Use Polars for CSV loading and daily aggregation |
+
+The installed `ml4t.backtest.analytics` signatures are recorded by the script environment: `sharpe_ratio(returns, risk_free_rate=0.0, annualize=True)`, `sortino_ratio(returns, risk_free_rate=0.0, annualize=True)`, `calmar_ratio(cagr_value, max_dd)`, and `max_drawdown(values)`. The library uses 252 days when annualization is enabled. This analysis calls its Sharpe and Sortino with `annualize=False` and multiplies by `sqrt(365.25)` to match the all-calendar-day grid. This equals the sample-mean/sample-standard-deviation formula. The library supplies maximum drawdown and Calmar.
+
+Run the analysis with:
+
+```bash
+UV_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/uvcache .venv/bin/python scripts/analyze_one_bar_nq_b0_b2_risk_20261012.py
+.venv/bin/pytest tests/test_one_bar_nq_b0_b2_risk_20261012.py -q
+```
+
+The analysis outputs are in [`risk_comparison_20261012`](../../run_log/one_bar_nq_stop_scaling_20261012/risk_comparison_20261012/): `metrics.json`, `metrics.csv`, and `monte_carlo.json`. The test suite has three tests for constant-series handling, risk-unit accounting, and bootstrap reproducibility.
+
+## Decision
+
+The observed dollar underperformance is **not mainly an unfilled $1,000 stop-risk budget**. B2 deployed close to its nominal risk budget. Lower MNQ contract exposure can reduce dollar P&L and the 2026 loss. After the MNQ launch date, B2 also has weaker win rate, profit factor, R expectancy, daily Sharpe, and Calmar than B0. The historical evidence therefore supports both lower point exposure and weaker risk-adjusted trade results, with the latter preventing a simple undersizing explanation.
+
+This is an exploratory historical accounting result. It does not approve B2, B0, or any other strategy for live trading.
diff --git a/scripts/analyze_one_bar_nq_b0_b2_risk_20261012.py b/scripts/analyze_one_bar_nq_b0_b2_risk_20261012.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..4ffecfba6e6cbdc9ea0082e15ea1a9ea1a53f480
--- /dev/null
+++ b/scripts/analyze_one_bar_nq_b0_b2_risk_20261012.py
@@ -0,0 +1,207 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Historical B0/B2 risk comparison; does not run a backtest."""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import hashlib
+import json
+from datetime import date
+from pathlib import Path
+
+import numpy as np
+import polars as pl
+from ml4t.backtest.analytics import calmar_ratio, max_drawdown, sharpe_ratio, sortino_ratio
+
+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
+OUT = ROOT / "run_log/one_bar_nq_stop_scaling_20261012/risk_comparison_20261012"
+SEED = 20261012
+REPS = 5000
+BLOCKS = (5, 20)
+START = "2013-01-01"
+END = "2026-07-14"
+LAUNCH = "2019-05-06"
+
+
+def sha256(path: Path) -> str:
+    return hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()
+
+
+def load_ledgers(base: str, leaf: str) -> tuple[pl.DataFrame, list[str]]:
+    paths = sorted((ROOT / base).glob(f"*/{leaf}/evaluation_trades.csv"))
+    if len(paths) != 14:
+        raise AssertionError(f"expected 14 annual files, found {len(paths)} under {base}")
+    frames = [pl.read_csv(path, try_parse_dates=False) for path in paths]
+    df = pl.concat(frames, how="diagonal_relaxed").with_columns(
+        pl.col("entry_time").str.slice(0, 10).alias("utc_entry_date"),
+        pl.col("pnl").cast(pl.Float64),
+    )
+    if df.filter(pl.col("status") != "closed").height:
+        raise AssertionError(f"non-closed ledger rows in {base}")
+    return df, [str(p.relative_to(ROOT)) for p in paths]
+
+
+def safe_sharpe(x: np.ndarray) -> float | None:
+    if len(x) < 2 or not np.isfinite(x).all() or np.std(x, ddof=1) == 0:
+        return None
+    return float(sharpe_ratio(x, risk_free_rate=0.0, annualize=False) * np.sqrt(365.25))
+
+
+def trade_stats(df: pl.DataFrame, label: str) -> dict:
+    p = df.get_column("pnl").to_numpy()
+    wins, losses = p[p > 0], p[p < 0]
+    loss_streak = best_loss_streak = 0
+    for value in p:
+        loss_streak = loss_streak + 1 if value < 0 else 0
+        best_loss_streak = max(best_loss_streak, loss_streak)
+    ans = {
+        "ledger": label, "trades": int(len(p)), "net_pnl_usd": float(p.sum()),
+        "win_rate": float((p > 0).mean()) if len(p) else None,
+        "ties": int((p == 0).sum()), "profit_factor": float(wins.sum() / abs(losses.sum())) if len(losses) and losses.sum() else None,
+        "average_win_usd": float(wins.mean()) if len(wins) else None,
+        "average_loss_usd": float(losses.mean()) if len(losses) else None,
+        "expectancy_usd_per_trade": float(p.mean()) if len(p) else None,
+        "worst_trade_usd": float(p.min()) if len(p) else None,
+        "max_consecutive_losses": best_loss_streak,
+    }
+    if "direction" in df.columns:
+        ans["by_direction"] = {
+            side: {"trades": int((df.get_column("direction") == side).sum()), "net_pnl_usd": float(p[df.get_column("direction").to_numpy() == side].sum())}
+            for side in sorted(df.get_column("direction").unique().to_list())
+        }
+    if "fees" in df.columns and "total_slippage_cost" in df.columns:
+        ans["fees_usd"] = float(df.get_column("fees").cast(pl.Float64).sum())
+        ans["slippage_usd"] = float(df.get_column("total_slippage_cost").cast(pl.Float64).sum())
+        ans["cost_drag_usd_per_trade"] = float((ans["fees_usd"] + ans["slippage_usd"]) / len(p)) if len(p) else None
+    if "nominal_risk_usd" in df.columns:
+        risk = df.get_column("nominal_risk_usd").cast(pl.Float64).to_numpy()
+        r = p / risk
+        qty = df.get_column("quantity").cast(pl.Float64).to_numpy()
+        ans.update({
+            "risk_unit_expectancy_r": float(r.mean()),
+            "risk_unit_win_rate": float((r > 0).mean()),
+            "risk_unit_worst_trade_r": float(r.min()),
+            "risk_budget_utilization_median": float(np.median(risk / 1000.0)),
+            "risk_budget_utilization_mean": float(np.mean(risk / 1000.0)),
+            "quantity_median_mnq": float(np.median(qty)),
+            "quantity_median_nq_equivalent": float(np.median(qty) / 10),
+            "share_trades_over_10_mnq": float(np.mean(qty > 10)),
+            "nominal_risk_over_1000_count": int(np.sum(risk > 1000)),
+        })
+        if "r_multiple" in df.columns:
+            ans["stored_r_multiple_max_abs_error"] = float(np.max(np.abs(r - df.get_column("r_multiple").cast(pl.Float64).to_numpy())))
+    return ans
+
+
+def equity_stats(daily_pnl: np.ndarray, risk_daily: np.ndarray, days: int) -> dict:
+    # Trade-entry-date closed P&L proxy, with a fixed illustrative $1m account.
+    equity = 1_000_000.0 + np.cumsum(daily_pnl)
+    dd_pct, peak_idx, trough_idx = max_drawdown(np.r_[1_000_000.0, equity])
+    peak_idx, trough_idx = max(0, peak_idx - 1), max(0, trough_idx - 1)
+    dd_usd = float(np.min(equity - np.maximum.accumulate(np.r_[1_000_000.0, equity])[:-1]))
+    cagr = float((equity[-1] / 1_000_000.0) ** (365.25 / days) - 1) if equity[-1] > 0 else None
+    ret = daily_pnl / 1_000_000.0
+    return {
+        "calendar_days": days, "net_pnl_usd": float(daily_pnl.sum()),
+        "daily_sharpe_usd": safe_sharpe(ret), "daily_sortino_usd": float(sortino_ratio(ret, 0.0, False) * np.sqrt(365.25)) if np.any(ret < 0) else None,
+        "daily_sharpe_r_units": safe_sharpe(risk_daily),
+        "max_drawdown_usd": dd_usd, "max_drawdown_pct": float(dd_pct),
+        "drawdown_peak_index": int(peak_idx), "drawdown_trough_index": int(trough_idx),
+        "cagr_1m_initial_capital": cagr,
+        "calmar_1m_initial_capital": float(calmar_ratio(cagr, float(dd_pct))) if cagr is not None and dd_pct != 0 else None,
+        "annualized_net_usd_over_max_drawdown_usd": float(daily_pnl.sum() * 365.25 / days / abs(dd_usd)) if dd_usd < 0 else None,
+    }
+
+
+def daily_panel(b0: pl.DataFrame, b2: pl.DataFrame, start: str, end: str) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, np.ndarray, list[str]]:
+    dates = pl.date_range(date.fromisoformat(start), date.fromisoformat(end), interval="1d", eager=True).dt.strftime("%Y-%m-%d").to_list()
+    grid = pl.DataFrame({"utc_entry_date": dates})
+    def daily(df: pl.DataFrame, val: str, alias: str) -> pl.DataFrame:
+        return df.filter((pl.col("utc_entry_date") >= start) & (pl.col("utc_entry_date") <= end)).group_by("utc_entry_date").agg(pl.col(val).sum().alias(alias))
+    b0d = grid.join(daily(b0, "pnl", "b0"), on="utc_entry_date", how="left").with_columns(pl.col("b0").fill_null(0.0))
+    b2d = grid.join(daily(b2, "pnl", "b2"), on="utc_entry_date", how="left").with_columns(pl.col("b2").fill_null(0.0))
+    b0r = grid.join(daily(b0.with_columns((pl.col("pnl") / 1000).alias("risk_r")), "risk_r", "b0r"), on="utc_entry_date", how="left").with_columns(pl.col("b0r").fill_null(0.0))
+    b2r = grid.join(daily(b2.with_columns((pl.col("pnl") / pl.col("nominal_risk_usd")).alias("risk_r")), "risk_r", "b2r"), on="utc_entry_date", how="left").with_columns(pl.col("b2r").fill_null(0.0))
+    return tuple(x.get_column(c).to_numpy() for x, c in [(b0d,"b0"),(b2d,"b2"),(b0r,"b0r"),(b2r,"b2r")]) + (dates,)
+
+
+def block_bootstrap(a: np.ndarray, b: np.ndarray, block: int, seed: int, thresholds: tuple[float, ...]) -> dict:
+    n = len(a)
+    nblocks = int(np.ceil(n / block))
+    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed + block)
+    starts = rng.integers(0, n, size=(REPS, nblocks))
+    idx = (starts[:, :, None] + np.arange(block)) % n
+    idx = idx.reshape(REPS, -1)[:, :n]
+    xa, xb = a[idx], b[idx]
+    def mdd(mat: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
+        cum = np.cumsum(mat, axis=1)
+        peaks = np.maximum.accumulate(np.concatenate([np.zeros((REPS, 1)), cum], axis=1), axis=1)[:, 1:]
+        return np.min(cum - peaks, axis=1)
+    def sharpe(mat: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
+        s = mat.std(axis=1, ddof=1)
+        return np.divide(mat.mean(axis=1), s, out=np.full(REPS, np.nan), where=s > 0) * np.sqrt(365.25)
+    da, db = mdd(xa), mdd(xb)
+    sa, sb = sharpe(xa), sharpe(xb)
+    delta = sb - sa
+    term_a, term_b = xa.sum(axis=1), xb.sum(axis=1)
+    def q(x: np.ndarray) -> list[float]:
+        return [float(v) for v in np.nanquantile(x, [0.05, 0.5, 0.95])]
+    return {
+        "block_days": block, "replicates": REPS, "terminal_net_5_50_95": {"B0": q(term_a), "B2": q(term_b)},
+        "prob_terminal_positive": {"B0": float(np.mean(term_a > 0)), "B2": float(np.mean(term_b > 0))},
+        "max_drawdown_50_95": {"B0": q(-da)[1:], "B2": q(-db)[1:]},
+        "prob_max_drawdown_exceeds_thresholds": {str(t): {"B0": float(np.mean(-da > t)), "B2": float(np.mean(-db > t))} for t in thresholds},
+        "annualized_sharpe_5_50_95": {"B0": q(sa), "B2": q(sb)},
+        "paired_sharpe_delta_B2_minus_B0_5_50_95": q(delta), "prob_B2_sharpe_gt_B0": float(np.mean(delta > 0)),
+    }
+
+
+def run() -> dict:
+    b0, b0paths = load_ledgers("run_log/one_bar_practical_1m_20261012/by_year", "native_full_tick_cost")
+    b2, b2paths = load_ledgers("run_log/one_bar_nq_stop_scaling_20261012/phase234/by_year", "B2_costed")
+    if b0.height != 5462 or not np.isclose(b0.get_column("pnl").sum(), 166107.92, atol=0.02):
+        raise AssertionError("B0 current annual ledgers do not match expected count/PnL")
+    if b2.height != 5459 or not np.isclose(b2.get_column("pnl").sum(), -142674.93, atol=0.02):
+        raise AssertionError("B2 current annual ledgers do not match independent review count/PnL")
+    b2_r_error = b2.select((pl.col("pnl") / pl.col("nominal_risk_usd") - pl.col("r_multiple")).abs().max()).item()
+    if b2_r_error > 1e-8:
+        raise AssertionError("B2 stored risk multiple does not reconcile to net P&L / nominal risk")
+    periods = {"full_historical": (START, END), "post_mnq_launch": (LAUNCH, END), "2020_2025": ("2020-01-01", "2025-12-31"), "2026_stress": ("2026-01-01", END), "pre_mnq_counterfactual": (START, "2019-05-05")}
+    results, mc = {}, {}
+    for name, (lo, hi) in periods.items():
+        x0 = b0.filter((pl.col("utc_entry_date") >= lo) & (pl.col("utc_entry_date") <= hi)).with_columns(pl.lit(1000.0).alias("nominal_risk_usd"))
+        x2 = b2.filter((pl.col("utc_entry_date") >= lo) & (pl.col("utc_entry_date") <= hi))
+        d0, d2, r0, r2, dates = daily_panel(x0, x2, lo, hi)
+        results[name] = {
+            "date_start": lo, "date_end": hi, "B0": trade_stats(x0, "B0"), "B2": trade_stats(x2, "B2"),
+            "B0_daily": equity_stats(d0, r0, len(dates)), "B2_daily": equity_stats(d2, r2, len(dates)),
+            "counterfactual_B2_scaled_to_1_NQ_equivalent": trade_stats(x2.with_columns(
+                (pl.col("pnl") * 10 / pl.col("quantity")).alias("pnl"),
+                (pl.col("nominal_risk_usd") * 10 / pl.col("quantity")).alias("nominal_risk_usd"),
+            ), "B2_linear_10_MNQ"),
+        }
+        if name in ("post_mnq_launch", "2026_stress"):
+            mc[name] = {}
+            for block in BLOCKS:
+                mc[name][f"usd_block_{block}"] = block_bootstrap(d0, d2, block, SEED, (5000.0,))
+                mc[name][f"risk_unit_block_{block}"] = block_bootstrap(r0, r2, block, SEED + 100, (5.0, 10.0))
+    return {
+        "status": "historical_review_only; NOT_APPROVED_FOR_LIVE", "seed": SEED, "replicates": REPS,
+        "source_cutoff_inclusive_utc": END, "pnl_attribution": "closed-trade net P&L assigned to UTC entry date; zeros on all other calendar days",
+        "annualization": "365.25 calendar days; rf=0; sample standard deviation", "periods": results, "monte_carlo": mc,
+        "source_files": {"B0": b0paths, "B2_costed": b2paths},
+        "source_sha256": {"B0": {p: sha256(ROOT / p) for p in b0paths}, "B2_costed": {p: sha256(ROOT / p) for p in b2paths}},
+        "limitations": ["BID-only CFD proxy; not dated CME futures", "pre-2019-05-06 MNQ is counterfactual", "annual B2 shards have documented GTC boundary leakage and duplicated entry fill", "trade-entry-day closed P&L is not native mark-to-market", "linear 1-NQ-equivalent B2 scaling is algebraic and ignores margin/impact", "moving-block bootstrap resamples this historical path and does not forecast future regimes", "2026 is observed stress evidence, not holdout"],
+    }
+
+
+if __name__ == "__main__":
+    OUT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    result = run()
+    (OUT / "metrics.json").write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=2, allow_nan=False) + "\n")
+    flat = []
+    for period, data in result["periods"].items():
+        for strategy in ("B0", "B2", "counterfactual_B2_scaled_to_1_NQ_equivalent"):
+            row = {"period": period, "strategy": strategy}
+            row.update(data[strategy])
+            flat.append(row)
+    pl.DataFrame(flat, infer_schema_length=None).write_csv(OUT / "metrics.csv")
+    (OUT / "monte_carlo.json").write_text(json.dumps(result["monte_carlo"], indent=2, allow_nan=False) + "\n")
diff --git a/tests/test_one_bar_nq_b0_b2_risk_20261012.py b/tests/test_one_bar_nq_b0_b2_risk_20261012.py
